# Agricultural Operations Report  
**Date:** October 15, 2023  
**Prepared by:** Green Valley Farms, Inc.  
**Location:** 2023 Harvest Lane, Springfield, IL 62701  

## Introduction  
This report outlines the current status of agricultural operations at Green Valley Farms, Inc., focusing on our crop production, livestock management, and irrigation systems as of the 2023 harvest season.

## Crop Production  
Green Valley Farms has successfully cultivated 150 acres of corn (Zea mays) and 100 acres of soybeans (Glycine max) this season, utilizing hybrid seeds from Pioneer Seeds. The corn yield is projected at 200 bushels per acre, while soybeans are expected to yield 50 bushels per acre. Our partnership with the University of Illinois Extension has enhanced our pest management strategies, specifically addressing the Spodoptera frugiperda infestation that impacted neighboring farms.

## Livestock Management  
We currently maintain a herd of 300 Angus cattle under the supervision of Dr. Emily Carter, our livestock veterinarian. The herd is fed a specialized diet formulated with feed sourced from ADM (Archer Daniels Midland) to optimize growth rates. Health monitoring is conducted weekly, with vaccinations administered in collaboration with the Illinois Department of Agriculture.

## Irrigation Systems  
The farm employs a state-of-the-art drip irrigation system designed by RainBird, covering 80% of our crop acreage. This system has improved water efficiency by 30%, crucial during this summer's drought conditions. Our water supply is sourced from the Sangamon River, managed under a permit issued by the Illinois Environmental Protection Agency (IEPA).

## Commodity Sales  
In terms of commodity sales, Green Valley Farms has secured contracts with Cargill and Archer Daniels Midland for the sale of our corn and soybeans at competitive rates. The projected revenue for the 2023 season is estimated at $1.2 million, with sales expected to commence in November 2023. 

## Conclusion  
Green Valley Farms remains committed to sustainable practices while maximizing yield and profitability. Our strategic partnerships and advanced farming techniques position us for continued success in the agricultural sector. Further evaluations will be conducted in early 2024 to assess the outcomes of this season's operations and plan for future initiatives.